  "bio": [
    "I am a Professor of Economics at the University of Exeter, working at the intersection of behavioural economics, global health, and development. My research uses field experiments and randomised trials to understand how people make decisions — and how those decisions can be improved through well-designed policy.",
    "My work spans cognitive performance and poverty, preference elicitation, wellbeing measurement, and the behavioural underpinnings of health outcomes. I have collaborated with governments, NGOs, and international organisations across Africa, Asia, and the Americas."
